# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Exception: a shared DEBUG-only keystore, committed on purpose so every
# machine signs debug/release-for-now builds with the same certificate.
# Google Sign-In's SHA-1 allowlist is per-certificate — without this, each
# developer's own auto-generated ~/.android/debug.keystore has a different
# fingerprint, and Sign-In breaks on every new machine until someone
# manually registers that machine's SHA-1 in Firebase. This is the
# well-known, non-secret Android debug key (password "android"), not a
# release signing key — safe to share within the team.
!app/debug.keystore
